// Where a value was, and a carrier the author asked for (docs/syntax.md, `LocationType`).
//
// Two options no other snapshot holds, and both are the host's to ask for rather than the
// grammar's to say: `LocationType` names an interface of the consumer's, and every rule
// whose value implements it is told the range it was read over; `Carrier` takes the choice
// away from `Auto`, which is what an author does when a construction of theirs must not run
// for input that is refused.
//
// The grammar also names what the host declares — `@Place` is the consumer's own type — so
// this snapshot is the one compiled under a real symbol resolver rather than the permissive
// one. What that resolver answers is in the file: which constructor of `Place` the captures
// fit, and that `Entry` may hold it.
//
// A configuration of lines, because a location is only interesting where a reader will be
// sent back to it: a key, a value, and the place of each.

trivia = { ' '* }

Config : @Entry[] = Entry*

Entry : @Entry = key: Name & '=' & value: Rest & eol => @(new Entry(key, value))

// Through a rule rather than straight from the characters. A value the engine builds inline
// from the spans its site recorded is handed no location at all today — the arguments there
// are the captured texts and nothing else — and a snapshot that does not compile is worse
// than no snapshot. Reported rather than carried here.
Name : @Place = w: Word => @(new Place(w))

Word : @string = t: ['a'..'z']+ => @(t)

Rest : @string = t: [^ '\r' | '\n']* => @(t)

parse Config
